{"anudataNita atmanepadam": [{"id": "anudAttaNita Atmanepadam", "headword": "अनुदात्तङित आत्मनेपदम्", "headword_slp1": "anudAttaNita Atmanepadam", "fold": "anudataNita atmanepadam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a root which has an indicatory अनुदात्त vowel (अनुदात्तेत्) or an indicatory ङ् (ङित्), the affixes are those of the आत्मनेपद।\n\nTerms: अनुदात्त-आत्मनेपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुदात्तङित आत्मनेपदम् १.३.१२", "१.३.१२", "१.३.१२ अनुदात्तङित आत्मनेपदम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anudAttaNita Atmanepadam १.३.१२", "१.३.१२", "१.३.१२ anudAttaNita Atmanepadam"]}], "anupasargadva": [{"id": "anupasargAdvA", "headword": "अनुपसर्गाद्वा", "headword_slp1": "anupasargAdvA", "fold": "anupasargadva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verb क्रम् the आत्मनेपद is optionally used, when it is not preceded by any preposition.\n\nTerms: आत्मनेपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुपसर्गाद्वा १.३.४३", "१.३.४३", "१.३.४३ अनुपसर्गाद्वा"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anupasargAdvA १.३.४३", "१.३.४३", "१.३.४३ anupasargAdvA"]}], "anupasargajYaH": [{"id": "anupasargAjjYaH", "headword": "अनुपसर्गाज्ज्ञः", "headword_slp1": "anupasargAjjYaH", "fold": "anupasargajYaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verb ज्ञा , when not preceded by any उपसर्ग , the terminations are of the आत्मनेपद , when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.\n\nTerms: आत्मनेपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुपसर्गाज्ज्ञः १.३.७६", "१.३.७६", "१.३.७६ अनुपसर्गाज्ज्ञः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anupasargAjjYaH १.३.७६", "१.३.७६", "१.३.७६ anupasargAjjYaH"]}], "anuparaByan kfYaH": [{"id": "anuparAByAM kfYaH", "headword": "अनुपराभ्यां कृञः", "headword_slp1": "anuparAByAM kfYaH", "fold": "anuparaByan kfYaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verb कृ 'to make' preceded by the अनु and पर , परस्मैपद is used, even the fruit of the action goes to the agent and when the sense is that of 'divulging' etc.\n\nTerms: परस्मैपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुपराभ्यां कृञः १.३.७९", "१.३.७९", "१.३.७९ अनुपराभ्यां कृञः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anuparAByAM kfYaH १.३.७९", "१.३.७९", "१.३.७९ anuparAByAM kfYaH"]}], "anupratigfRasca": [{"id": "anupratigfRaSca", "headword": "अनुप्रतिगृणश्च", "headword_slp1": "anupratigfRaSca", "fold": "anupratigfRasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the case of the verb गृ preceded by अनु and प्रति and meaning 'to encourage by repeating', the person who was the agent of the prior action, which is repeated, is called सम्प्रदान।\n\nTerms: कारक-सम्प्रदान", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुप्रतिगृणश्च १.४.४१", "१.४.४१", "१.४.४१ अनुप्रतिगृणश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anupratigfRaSca १.४.४१", "१.४.४१", "१.४.४१ anupratigfRaSca"]}], "anukaraRan canitiparam": [{"id": "anukaraRaM cAnitiparam", "headword": "अनुकरणं चानितिपरम्", "headword_slp1": "anukaraRaM cAnitiparam", "fold": "anukaraRan canitiparam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A word imitative of sounds is also called गति when it is not followed by the word इति।\n\nTerms: गति-संज्ञा", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुकरणं चानितिपरम् १.४.६२", "१.४.६२", "१.४.६२ अनुकरणं चानितिपरम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anukaraRaM cAnitiparam १.४.६२", "१.४.६२", "१.४.६२ anukaraRaM cAnitiparam"]}], "anurlaksaRe": [{"id": "anurlakzaRe", "headword": "अनुर्लक्षणे", "headword_slp1": "anurlakzaRe", "fold": "anurlaksaRe", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The word अनु , when it denotes a sign, is called कर्म-प्रवचनीय।\n\nTerms: कर्मप्रवचनीय-संज्ञा", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अनुर्लक्षणे १.४.८४", "१.४.८४", "१.४.८४ अनुर्लक्षणे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anurlakzaRe १.४.८४", "१.४.८४", "१.४.८४ anurlakzaRe"]}], "anuryatsamaya